      "text": "We are given that $a_n = a_{n - 1} a_{n + 1}$ for all $n \\ge 2.$  Dividing both sides by $a_{n - 1}a_{n + 1}$, we get\n\\[\\frac{1}{a_n} = \\frac{1}{a_{n - 1}} + \\frac{1}{a_{n + 1}}.\\]There are 17 different numbers in the sequence $\\frac{1}{a_2},\\frac{1}{a_3},\\dots,\\frac{1}{a_{2009}},\\frac{1}{a_1}$, each occurring twice, so their sum must be the same number, namely the sum\n\\[\\frac{1}{a_2} + \\frac{1}{a_3} + \\dots + \\frac{1}{a_{2009}} + \\frac{1}{a_1} = \\frac{1}{a_1} + \\frac{1}{a_2} + \\frac{1}{a_3} + \\dots + \\frac{1}{a_{2009}} + \\frac{1}{a_1}.\\]This means that $\\frac{1}{a_1} + \\frac{1}{a_2} + \\dots + \\frac{1}{a_{2009}} = \\frac{1}{a_2} + \\frac{1}{a_3} + \\dots + \\frac{1}{a_{2009}} + \\frac{1}{a_1}.$  But\n\\[\\frac{1}{a_n} = \\frac{1}{a_{n-1}} + \\frac{1}{a_{n + 1}},\\]so\n\\[\\frac{1}{a_2} + \\frac{1}{a_3} + \\dots + \\frac{1}{a_{2009}} = \\frac{1}{a_2} + \\frac{1}{a_3} + \\dots + \\frac{1}{a_{2009}} + \\frac{1}{a_1} = \\frac{1}{a_1} + \\frac{1}{a_2} + \\frac{1}{a_3} + \\dots + \\frac{1}{a_{2009}} + \\frac{1}{a_1}.\\]Then $a_1 = \\boxed{2}$.\n\nThe answer is: 2",
